5,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw0MTAwNjQ0ODU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/needs%20testing","name":"needs testing","color":"ffcc44","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-11-16T04:29:45Z","updated_at":"2025-11-18T11:48:38Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproduced on `4.6-dev4` and `4.5.1`\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.dev4 - macOS Tahoe (26.1.0) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M1 Max (Apple7) - Apple M1 Max (10 threads) - 64.00 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen the project setting `application/run/max_fps` is nonzero, the editor—not just the project—is limited to the specified frame rate.\n\nI would expect the editor's frame rate to be independent of project settings. The editor should either ignore the setting or have its own equivalent in Editor Settings.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a new project and set `max_fps` to a low value (eg. 10) in Project Settings\n- Save and reload the project (Project → Reload Current Project)\n\nEditor now runs with its frame rate capped at the set value.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nCouldn't get Github upload to work but the setup is very simple.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112839/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112839/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}